    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's look at this code:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "1console.log(\"Start\");\n2console.log(\"Middle\");\n3console.log(\"End\");"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Before you run it, think for a while and ask yourself:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "\"In what order will the messages appear?\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "When you run the code, the output will be:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Start\nMiddle\nEnd"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "You probably already guessed the output. After all, JavaScript executes the codes line by line, one after the other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "JS can't execute the next line before completing the first one."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
